  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data-collection survey on building resilient and cohesive communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda is facing mounting pressure following the arrival of nearly 8,000 returnees from the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) in 2025, straining already limited services in border districts. Economically fragile host communities struggle to absorb returnees, increasing pressure on essential services and risks of social tension. These challenges are exacerbated by recurring climate-induced disasters in the Northern and Western Provinces, causing displacement, loss of life, and destruction of homes, and by gaps in up-to-date data on the needs of returnees and host communities.In response, the project aims to strengthen social cohesion and build resilient, peaceful communities by applying an evidence based and community driven approach. It will identify needs and potential friction points through tools such as the Peacebuilding Needs Assessment, develop Community Action Plans through inclusive joint committees, test the effectiveness of the combined &#x201c;Peacebuilding x Disaster Risk Reduction&#x201d; approach through pilot initiatives, and ultimately formulate a nationwide scalable Community Resilience Enhancement Package to inform future JICA cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
